            <title>[LU-20848] lnetctl net show returns success for invalid options</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20848</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;"lnetctl net show --bogus"&lt;/tt&gt; prints an error but exits with status 0.&lt;br/&gt;
This is incorrectly passing failing tests in our internal tests.&lt;/p&gt;



&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;
$ lnetctl net show --bogus
net show: show networks
        --net: net name (e.g. tcp0) to filter on
        --verbose: display detailed output per network. Optional argument of &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;'2'&lt;/span&gt; outputs more stats
$ echo $?
0
 
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;</description>
